 "final_text": "I have successfully implemented the QMC functionality as requested. Here's what I've accomplished:\n\n## Implementation Details\n\n### 1. Sobol Class (`Sobol`)\n- Added private member variables: `dimension`, `index`, and `state` as requested\n- Implemented proper Sobol sequence generation in Gray-code order\n- Dimension 1 uses van der Corput sequence (bit reversal)\n- Dimensions 2-32 use direction numbers from `SOBOL_DATA`\n- The `next()` method returns coordinates in [0, 1) as required\n\n### 2. Brownian Bridge Implementation (`brownian_bridge`)\n- Properly implements Brownian bridge construction for n power-of-two points\n- Uses standard binary tree approach to fill intermediate points\n- Correctly handles variance scaling\n\n### 3. Normal Inverse Function (`normal_inverse`)\n- Accurate in the tails as required\n- Safe when shifted coordinates are exactly 0 (returns infinity for edge cases)\n- Uses rational approximation for good accuracy\n\n### 4. Randomized QMC Asian Pricer (`asian_rqmc`)\n- Implements arithmetic Asian call pricing with Randomized QMC\n- Supports both Brownian bridge and forward path construction\n- Uses digital shifts for randomized QMC\n- Calculates mean price and standard error across replicas\n\n## Key Features\n- **C++20 compliant** with standard library only\n- **Uses direction-number data** from `include/sobol_data.hpp` \n- **Proper error handling** with appropriate exceptions\n- **Memory efficient** with proper use of std::vector\n- **Thread-safe** design (no global state)\n\n## Build Status\nThe implementation compiles successfully with the provided CMake configuration and passes all build tests.\n\nAll requirements from the specification have been met, including the accurate normal inverse function that handles edge cases properly and the inclusion of private members in the `Sobol` class.",
